# Structure Lock — content-only edits

The website structure is final. Your job is rewriting words, not rebuilding the site.

## Never do any of the following (even if it seems like an improvement)

- Do NOT add, remove, rename, or reorder routes in `src/App.tsx`.
- Do NOT create new pages, new components, or new files unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do NOT edit any `.css` file, Tailwind classes, animation code, motion hooks (`usePageMotion`, `usePublisherMotion`), or anything in `src/components/ui/`.
- Do NOT change JSX structure: keep the same elements, wrappers, class names, component props, section order, and markup. Only replace the human-readable strings inside them.
- Do NOT change the TypeScript types/shapes in `src/data/blog.ts`, `src/data/verticals.ts`, or `src/data/site.ts`. You may edit field VALUES and add new array ITEMS that match the existing type exactly.
- Do NOT touch `vite.config.ts`, `tsconfig*`, `package.json`, deployment workflow, `_redirects`, or `src/main.tsx`.
- Do NOT remove or restructure the `<Seo />` component usage — only edit the string values passed to it.

## Where content lives (the ONLY things you edit)

| Content | File(s) |
| --- | --- |
| Page copy (headlines, paragraphs, button labels, FAQ text) | string literals inside `src/pages/*.tsx` |
| Blog posts | `src/data/blog.ts` (edit posts / append new posts matching `BlogPost` type) |
| Vertical copy + keywords | `src/data/verticals.ts` (edit values; keep slugs and categories stable) |
| Tagline, nav labels | `src/data/site.ts` (values only) |
| Meta titles/descriptions/keywords/JSON-LD | `Seo` props inside each page; `index.html` defaults |
| Sitemap entries for new blog posts | `public/sitemap.xml` |

## If a rewrite seems to require a structural change

Stop and tell the user what you'd want to change and why. Do not make the change yourself.

## Slugs and URLs

Existing blog and vertical slugs are live URLs. Never rename an existing `slug`. New blog posts get new kebab-case slugs and a matching `<url>` entry in `public/sitemap.xml`.
